Title: The Conservatory
Order: 7
Production Code: 1x07

INT. VANCE ESTATE - CONSERVATORY - DAY

AMB: a garden party murmuring in the next room

[[Reuel Briggs]] leads [[Dianthe Lusk]] away from the crush of admirers to the quiet of the conservatory.

REUEL BRIGGS
I have nothing to offer a wife but debt and an unfinished degree.

DIANTHE LUSK
You have more than that.

REUEL BRIGGS
Marry me anyway.

DIANTHE LUSK
(a real smile)
Yes.

INT. LIVINGSTON'S ROOMS - NIGHT

AMB: a low fire

Weeks later. Reuel, anxious, comes to [[Aubrey Livingston]] for help — every position he's applied for has mysteriously fallen through.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Briggs — do you think anyone knows or suspects your origin?

REUEL BRIGGS
(steady)
I've wondered if that's the reason.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
This prejudice closes doors in good men's faces. I'm ashamed of my own section for it.

(beat)

There's an English expedition sailing for Meroe. They need a physician who isn't afraid of ruins. Two years' contract, and a fortune in it if it goes well — and some good it might do the race, if the histories it's chasing turn out true.

REUEL BRIGGS
And Dianthe?

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Marry her before you go. Molly and I will keep her like a sister while you're away. I give you my word.

They clasp hands on it. Neither says what either one is actually thinking.
